Real DevOps Errors (and How to Fix Them Fast) 🚀

⚠️ Error: npm install works locally, but fails in CI/CD.
✅ Solution: Cache dependencies in your pipeline & pin Node.js + package versions.

⚠️ Error: Docker image build takes 20+ minutes.
✅ Solution: Use multi-stage builds & a smaller base image (e.g., alpine).

⚠️ Error: Kubernetes pod stuck in CrashLoopBackOff.
✅ Solution: Check logs with kubectl logs <pod> → fix env vars/DB connection/health probes.

⚠️ Error: “Permission denied” when deploying to cloud.
✅ Solution: Verify IAM roles → apply least privilege policies instead of admin access.

⚠️ Error: Secrets exposed in Git history.
✅ Solution: Rotate the key immediately 🔑 + use Vault/Secrets Manager to manage credentials.

⚠️ Error: Pipeline fails because of missing DATABASE_URL.
✅ Solution: Store env variables in a secure place (GitHub Actions Secrets, Jenkins Credentials, AWS SSM).

⚠️ Error: terraform apply works on one machine, but breaks on another.
✅ Solution: Use remote backend (S3, GCS, Terraform Cloud) for consistent state management.

⚠️ Error: On-call wakes you up at 2 AM for 100+ alerts 🚨
✅ Solution: Set proper thresholds, group alerts, and silence noisy/non-actionable alerts.

⚠️ Error: Rollback fails after a bad release.
✅ Solution: Use blue-green or canary deployments → test rollback steps before production.

💡 Takeaway: Real DevOps is less about writing YAML and more about solving problems under pressure. Automate, monitor, and test everything.
